  "final_message": "I am waiting for `npm test` to finish running in the background.\nI am waiting for `typecheck` and `arch` to complete.\nI am waiting for the contract verification check to finish running in the background.\nI am waiting for `git diff` to complete.\nTo fix the `ARCH-4` contract failures with downstream consumers while still supporting the renamed fields:\n\n### Changes\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L62)**:\n   - Included the new fields `createdAt` and `amountCents` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7).\n   - Retained `placedAt` and `totalCents` on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7) as backwards-compatible aliases so existing consumers (`analytics-ingest` and `billing-service`) continue to satisfy their contract requirements.\n   - Populated both new names and legacy aliases in the [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L45) factory function.\n\n2. **Tests**:\n   - Updated [`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/test/app.test.ts#L21-L34) and [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w7/r/orders-service/test/adapters.test.ts#L46-L53) to verify that both `amountCents` / `totalCents` and `createdAt` / `placedAt` are emitted on the event.\n\n`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, and `npm run arch` all pass.\n",
